# Psalms of Solomon — Psalm 15 — The EMET Bible (Literal)
**Translator:** EMET | **Source:** Greek MS (Codex Vindobonensis) | **Section:** God's Protection of the Devout; Destruction of Sinners

---

**15:1** When I was in distress I called upon the name of the LORD;
I hoped for the help of the God of Jacob, and he saved me.

**15:2** For thou art the hope and refuge of the poor, O God;
who is there to save the poor and the weak, O God, if not thee?

**15:3** Thou wilt answer, O LORD, the prayer of the poor;
thy words are righteous, O God, and thou wilt not cut off the hope of those who trust thee.

**15:4** When thou art praised, who will fear thee?
For all that thou hast made will give praise to thee when thou judgest.

**15:5** For the devout are in thy hand;
thine is the hand that saves — thou wilt never forsake them.

**15:6** But the fear of the LORD is upon the righteous ones;
they will not stumble in the darkness.

**15:7** The devout of the LORD will not be afraid of darkness;
but they will make appeal with hymns, praising the name of their God.

**15:8** And the LORD will hear the prayer of those who love him;
and in the time of their prayer he will not set them aside.

**15:9** Blessed is the LORD who has mercy on those who love him in truth.

**15:10** But sinners will be taken away into eternal destruction,
and the memory of them will not be found any more.

**15:11** But the mercy of the LORD is upon those who love him in truth;
and the LORD will help the righteous ones.

**15:12** For our refuge is in the LORD our savior forever;
the righteous will not be moved by the nations,

**15:13** but will be guided by the fear of God,
for God [himself] is the defender of the weak.

---

*EMET notes: Translated from the Greek (Codex Vindobonensis). Hyphenated compounds preserve construct chains. Bracketed words [thus] are implied by grammar but absent from the surface text.*
